<%# What this quarter pays, for whoever is looking at it.

    This was inside the finalize block, which is `current_user.admin?` - so the person entering the
    grades could not see the summary of what they add up to, while the person who only presses the
    button could. Reported as not seeing the grades summary card, and the gate was in the wrong place:
    the **summary is information** for anyone who can open the page, and only the **action** is
    administrative. They should never have been one block.

    Split by reason because that is how the money is written: DistributeEarnings creates one transaction
    per reason, so these three subtotals are what lands on the students' statements rather than an
    arbitrary grouping.

    Its own element id, so a save refreshes it along with the figures it summarises. %>
<%= tag.section id: "earnings-summary", class: "tw-card mt-6 p-5",
                aria: { labelledby: "earnings-summary-heading" } do %>
  <p id="earnings-summary-heading" class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-900">
    What this quarter pays
  </p>
  <p class="mt-1 max-w-2xl text-sm text-slate-600">
    From the grades and attendance entered above. Nothing is paid until the quarter is finalized.
  </p>

  <dl class="mt-3 max-w-xs space-y-1 text-sm">
    <% { attendance: "Attendance", math: "Math", reading: "Reading" }.each do |key, label| %>
      <div class="flex justify-between gap-4">
        <dt class="text-slate-600"><%= label %></dt>
        <dd class="tabular-nums text-slate-900">
          <%= number_to_currency(earnings.totals_by_reason[key] / 100.0) %>
        </dd>
      </div>
    <% end %>

    <div class="flex justify-between gap-4 border-t border-slate-200 pt-1">
      <dt class="font-medium text-slate-900">
        Total for <%= pluralize(earnings.student_count, "student") %>
      </dt>
      <dd class="font-semibold tabular-nums text-slate-900" data-testid="summary-total">
        <%= number_to_currency(earnings.total_cents / 100.0) %>
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
<% end %>
